truction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:675f70e7e79d2a63dc37a73f9d35952abd59c1a833eecee086b7b47cc6838d74","file":"preprints/A-classification-of-finite-Euclidean-Ramsey-configurations-September-23-2026/build/sections/02-tensors.tex","line":144,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"b8c5ae13ba4618a63f00be4ba8db4b48a1dd6d6a11ec0e01927591288d0ccd4e","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-classification-of-finite-Euclidean-Ramsey-configurations-September-23-2026/build/sections/02-tensors.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:675f70e7e79d2a63dc37a73f9d35952abd59c1a833eecee086b7b47cc6838d74","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-classification-of-finite-Euclidean-Ramsey-configurations-September-23-2026/build/sections/02-tensors.tex#L144"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{alg:necessity}\nIf~\\eqref{alg:tensor} has no solution, then there is an integer $r_0\\geq2$\nsuch that every $\\R^D$ admits an $r_0$-coloring with no monochromatic\ncongruent copy of $A$.  In particular, every Euclidean Ramsey set\nsatisfies the matrix condition of Theorem~\\ref{thm:classification}."}
